The nasals {{IPAblink|m}} and {{IPAblink|n}} likely had syllabic forms: {{IPAblink|m̩}} and {{IPAblink|n̩}}. Jacobs possibly notes that the plosives also have voiced allophones, as {{IPAblink|b}}, {{IPAblink|d}}, {{IPAblink|ɡ}}, {{IPAblink|ɡʷ}}, {{IPAblink|ɢ}}, and {{IPAblink|ɢʷ}}. Banks also notes that {{IPA|/h/, /hʷ/, /dz/, /dʒ/}}, and {{IPA|/ɸʷ/}} may have been allophones.<ref name="banks" />

